# MaCSad public hero

The hero states the publication promise and renders the honest empty baseline.

## Component PublicHero:
    View:
        css ".hero { padding: clamp(64px,9vw,118px) clamp(22px,5vw,72px) 72px; background: radial-gradient(circle at 85% 15%,rgba(216,255,114,.14),transparent 30%), #102c3b; } .hero-inner { max-width: 1240px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(280px,100%),1fr)); gap: clamp(40px,7vw,100px); align-items: end; margin: auto; } .overline { margin: 0 0 18px; color: #d8ff72; font: 800 11px/1 ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; } h1 { max-width: 800px; margin: 0; color: #f9f6ed; font: 700 clamp(44px,7vw,86px)/.98 Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.045em; } .hero-copy { max-width: 680px; margin: 24px 0 0; color: #b9cbd1; font-size: clamp(15px,1.6vw,18px); line-height: 1.7; } .issue-card { padding: 25px; color: #1a333e; background: #d8ff72; border-radius: 16px; box-shadow: 0 22px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.18); } .issue-card small { display: block; margin-bottom: 28px; font: 800 10px/1 ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; } .issue-card strong { display: block; font: 750 31px/1.05 Georgia, serif; } .issue-card p { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.55; }"
        section [class="hero"]:
            div [class="hero-inner"]:
                div:
                    p [class="overline"]: "Mathematics × computer science"
                    h1: "Discovery should be inspectable."
                    p [class="hero-copy"]: "MaCSad is a framework for directed auto-research. Questions become controlled processes; claims become public only after their evidence and review trail are sealed."
                aside [class="issue-card"]:
                    small: "Baseline edition · 001"
                    strong: "No discoveries published yet."
                    p: "This is the honest empty state while the research and publication pipelines are being connected."
